# riir-reflexer local configuration — the template for `.env`.
#
# Copy:  cp .env.example .env   then fill in real values.
# `.env` is gitignored — NEVER commit it, never paste its values anywhere else.
# (This is a PUBLIC repo: a leaked value is leaked for good.)
#
# Nothing sources `.env` automatically — export what you need first:
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a

# ── Cloudflare ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN — the one token wrangler uses (deploy).
#   Get: CF dashboard → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token → Custom →
#        Account · Workers Scripts · Edit (nothing else).
#   Used by: manual deploys of the two Workers under cloudflare/
#   (`cd cloudflare/reflexer-worker && npx wrangler deploy`) and
#   scripts/vmint-keygen.sh (`wrangler secret put`). The CI mirror
#   .github/workflows/reflexer_worker.yml (main only) maps the repo secret
#   CF_DEPLOY_API_TOKEN to it. The crates/CLI never read it.
#   Absent → wrangler falls back to your `wrangler login` OAuth.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# ── Signing keys (src/bin/reflexer.rs, src/record.rs) ───────────────────────
# REFLEXER_SIGN_KEY: 64-hex ed25519 seed for `reflexer sign` (minting a
#   PUBLIC-RELEASE vessel). Precedence: --key > --key-file > this env.
#   Absent and no flag → refuses (fail-closed).
#   Generate: `scripts/vmint-keygen.sh --root <out-file>` writes a fresh seed
#   to a 0600 file, or `openssl genpkey -algorithm ed25519` (OpenSSL 3).
#   Prefer --key-file over the env for anything long-lived.
# REFLEXER_SIGN_KEY=
# REFLEXER_SUBMISSION_KEY: PATH to the per-machine 32-byte trajectory
#   submission seed. Default ~/.config/reflexer/submission.ed25519 (0600,
#   created on first use). Its public half rides the manifest.
# REFLEXER_SUBMISSION_KEY=

# ── Worker secrets (pushed with wrangler, NOT read from .env) ───────────────
# VESSEL_MINT_SEED: the vessel-mint Worker's online-tier Ed25519 mint seed.
#   Generated AND pushed in one step — the seed never reaches stdout or .env:
#     scripts/vmint-keygen.sh vessel-mint [SECRET_NAME] [--env <env>]
#   (default secret name VESSEL_MINT_SEED; runs `wrangler secret put` with
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN or OAuth). CF secrets are write-only:
#   a lost seed is recovered by ROOT re-delegation, never read back.
#   The reflexer-worker itself has zero secrets and zero bindings.

# ── Bench knob ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAX_LOAD: load-average ceiling for examples/measure.rs (refuses above it).
# MAX_LOAD=6.0
